invariant: INV-16
file: src/aead_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: pass_hashing absorbs the last block of its pass twice and never the
  block before it, so the tag of every message of two passes or more is
  wrong. The ten double rounds absorb 30 of a pass's 32 blocks, and the two
  after the loop are the rest. bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test compares the one
  pass with the two-pass AEAD; the script builds it for x86-64 and runs it
  under qemu-x86_64, because the file has a body there alone.

--- old
    poly1305_wide_block(&a, &k, last);
--- new
    poly1305_wide_block(&a, &k, last + POLY1305_BLOCK);
